WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.640
A 30-gram mouse and a 70-kilogram human.

2
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.560
The human is more than 2,000 times heavier.

3
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:19.340
Yet a widely used fit for mammals predicts it burns only about 340 times the energy.

4
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:27.460
Each kilogram of mouse burns about seven times more than each kilogram of human. Why?

5
00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:31.413
Everything a body exchanges crosses its surface.

6
00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:34.673
Model a cell as an ideal cube.

7
00:00:35.573 --> 00:00:41.433
Double its side, and the area grows four times, but the volume grows eight times.

8
00:00:42.293 --> 00:00:49.873
So the surface area to volume ratio halves, from 0.6 to 0.3 per micrometre.

9
00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:53.853
These cubes are illustrative, not measured cells.

10
00:00:54.683 --> 00:01:00.543
Diffusion is the net spread of molecules from crowded places to less crowded ones.

11
00:01:01.323 --> 00:01:06.883
In a simple model, the typical time is the distance squared, divided by two times

12
00:01:06.883 --> 00:01:08.103
the diffusion coefficient.

13
00:01:09.003 --> 00:01:15.063
For a small solute in water, 10 micrometres takes about 0.05 seconds.

14
00:01:15.883 --> 00:01:18.543
One centimetre takes about 14 hours.

15
00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:24.707
Animals and plants meet the same geometry with the same four answers.

16
00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:30.987
Flattening keeps every cell near the outside, in a planarian flatworm and a leaf

17
00:01:30.987 --> 00:01:37.067
blade. Folding packs surface into a small space, in the alveoli of the mammalian

18
00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:38.987
lung and inside a leaf.

19
00:01:40.107 --> 00:01:45.327
Branching divides the airways again and again, and splits leaf veins into finer

20
00:01:45.327 --> 00:01:52.507
veins. Bulk flow moves a whole fluid, and diffusion still covers the last few micrometres.

21
00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:00.740
A widely quoted fit for mammals says basal rate is 70 times mass to the power 0.75

22
00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.520
in kilocalories a day.

23
00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:08.940
That gives a 30-gram mouse about 5 kilocalories a day, and a 70-kilogram adult

24
00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.180
human about 1,700.

25
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:17.380
Per kilogram, that is about 168 for the mouse and 24 for the human.

26
00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:23.520
The exponent is below 1, so rate per kilogram falls as animals get bigger.

27
00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:28.180
Treat three-quarters as a fit, not a law.

28
00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:34.940
White and Seymour found a mammalian exponent near two-thirds once body temperature

29
00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:36.840
and digestive state were controlled.

30
00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:43.900
With two-thirds, the mouse's advantage per kilogram becomes about 13 times, not 7.

31
00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.320
The cause of the exponent is still debated.

32
00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:54.760
Keep this rule: in larger bodies surface falls behind volume, so flow carries

33
00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:58.200
material, and diffusion covers the last few micrometres.
